  ('ML-NEW-029-gancho-drone-usar-funcao-elementos', 'Create an approximately 8-second ultra-realistic vertical 9:16 POV video with fast, dynamic, viral social-media energy.

POV RULE:
This must be true first-person visual logic.
The camera is the eyes of the person standing on a Brazilian sidewalk.
Do not show the camera wearer’s face.
Only the POV hands and forearms may appear.
The hands must always spatially belong to the camera wearer.

ELEMENT AUTHORITY:
The ORIGINAL PRODUCT ELEMENT is the sole source of truth for the product:
same exact geometry,
same exact proportions,
same exact materials,
same exact colors,
same exact visible labels,
same exact design,
same exact scale.

The SCENE/COMPOSITION ELEMENT provides:
Brazilian sidewalk environment,
daylight,
street context,
box placement,
POV composition,
and spatial relationships.

If there is any conflict, the ORIGINAL PRODUCT ELEMENT always wins.
Do not redesign the product.
Do not replace it with a similar item.
Do not invent parts or accessories.
Do not morph it after the box opens.

CORE EVENT:
The video begins with the POV person on a Brazilian sidewalk looking up.
A small distant satellite is visible high in the sky as a brief opening visual detail.
A realistic delivery drone is the actual delivery vehicle.
The drone carries a cardboard parcel and quickly releases it.
The box falls fast and lands on the Brazilian sidewalk.
The POV person immediately reaches down, grabs the box, opens it, and reveals the exact attached product inside.

STYLE:
Fast, dynamic, viral pacing.
5 to 6 microtakes in approximately 8 seconds.
Quick hard cuts.
No dissolve.
No morph.
No cinematic polish.
Real smartphone energy.
The event must feel immediate and shareable.

MICROTAKE STRUCTURE:

0.0–0.9s — SKY OPENING
POV shot looking upward from the sidewalk.
Blue daytime sky.
A tiny distant satellite is visible high above only as a small secondary orbital object.
A delivery drone enters lower in the sky carrying a cardboard parcel.
Camera has natural handheld energy and slight autofocus correction.

0.9–1.9s — DRONE OVERHEAD
Hard cut to a stronger upward POV angle.
The drone hovers above the Brazilian sidewalk, clearly carrying the parcel.
The parcel is attached in a simple physically believable way.
The drone quickly releases the box.
No sci-fi mechanics.
No spaceship behavior.

1.9–3.0s — FAST FALL AND LANDING
Hard cut to a downward-following POV angle as the box drops fast toward the sidewalk.
The box falls with believable gravity and speed, then lands on the concrete pavement with a firm impact and a small bounce or skid.
The camera wearer reacts naturally by dipping the view downward toward the box.
The drone exits upward or off-frame naturally.

3.0–4.4s — HANDS GRAB THE BOX
Hard cut to a lower POV angle.
The camera wearer crouches or leans down.
Both hands reach into frame and grab the parcel.
Exactly five fingers per visible hand.
Correct thumb placement, real grip pressure, real contact shadows.
The box remains a normal cardboard shipping box.

4.4–6.0s — OPENING THE PARCEL
Hard cut to a tight POV close-up.
The hands open the top cardboard flaps using only physically plausible box behavior.
No magical opening.
No hidden complex mechanism.
The flaps separate, bend and stay open.
The interior reveal begins.
The exact attached product becomes visible inside.

6.0–8.0s — PRODUCT REVEAL
Hard cut to the final hero POV reveal.
The hands either lift the exact product slightly out of the box or hold the opened box toward the camera, depending on product size.
If the product is compact enough, lift it naturally with proper support.
If the product is larger or awkward, keep it partially inside the box and reveal it clearly without forcing impossible handling.
Use a brief handheld push-in or rack focus onto the product.
End with the product clearly readable and unchanged.

BRAZILIAN SIDEWALK:
Believable contemporary Brazilian street context.
Concrete sidewalk, curb, gate or front wall, garage entrance, house façade or mixed residential/commercial surroundings.
Natural neighborhood details.
No luxury fantasy.
No sterile AI environment.
No caricature.

DRONE:
Realistic delivery drone.
Functional, contemporary, plausible size.
It only needs to arrive, carry the parcel, release it, and leave.
Do not overdesign it.
No sci-fi spaceship look.
No impossible mechanics.

CAMERA:
Recent smartphone main camera.
1x.
Approximately 24–26mm equivalent.
Vertical 9:16.
Natural handheld.
Real autofocus.
Subtle auto-exposure changes in daylight.
Natural smartphone sharpening.
Subtle sensor noise.
Real motion blur.
No Portrait Mode.
No fake bokeh.
No perfect gimbal.
No cinematic dolly.
No fake HDR.
No studio glow.

PRODUCT FIDELITY:
The exact attached product must remain identical across the whole reveal.
Do not change color, label, proportions, packaging logic, material finish or scale.
Do not generate a similar replacement after the flaps open.
The original Product Element remains source of truth at all times.

VISIBLE-GEOMETRY-ONLY:
Do not invent product functions or mechanisms.
Only show what is visually supported by the reference.
If the product has unclear geometry, keep the reveal simple:
show it inside the box,
lift it carefully,
or present it toward the camera without using unverified moving parts.

HAND ANATOMY:
Exactly five fingers per visible hand.
Correct joints.
Correct thumb placement.
Natural nails and cuticles.
Real skin folds.
Real grip pressure.
No clipping.
No merged fingers.
No fingers passing through the box or product.

PHYSICS:
Respect gravity, inertia, friction, contact, support and occlusion.
The parcel must fall downward naturally.
The parcel lands and stays where it lands.
The hands must physically grip the box before opening it.
The product does not teleport out of the box.
The product is revealed only after the flaps open.
Nothing changes size when approaching the camera.

FAIL-SAFE:
If the fast drop threatens realism, keep the drop quick but slightly shorter and lower, then transfer energy to sound, impact, camera dip and quick cuts.
If opening the box threatens product fidelity, simplify the motion:
open the flaps,
pause briefly,
show the product inside,
then reveal it with a smaller lift.
The camera may become more dynamic.
The product must remain exact.

AUDIO:
Natural Brazilian street ambience,
light neighborhood background,
drone buzzing during arrival,
cardboard impact on concrete,
box flap sounds,
hand handling sounds.
No music required.

Dialogue: sem fala.', NULL),
  ('ML-NEW-030-brincos', 'Create a premium jewelry showcase video using the provided reference image. Start with the original framing. As the camera slowly zooms in toward the earrings, the model gently lifts one hand and naturally sweeps her hair behind the ear, carefully tucking it behind the ear to reveal the entire earring. Her movement must be elegant, delicate, realistic, and fluid, like a luxury jewelry commercial. After tucking her hair behind her ear, she keeps her hand lowered and slightly turns her head to showcase the earring clearly. The camera continues a smooth, gradual zoom until the earring becomes the main focal point, capturing the sparkling stones, intricate details, gold settings, and realistic reflections in sharp focus. Preserve the exact same adult female model, facial features, hairstyle, skin texture, clothing, and original earrings from the reference image. Keep the jewelry identical in design, shape, size, and color. Natural hand anatomy, realistic fingers, subtle facial expressions, soft daylight, shallow depth of field, photorealistic quality. No cuts, no scene changes, no jewelry alterations, no extra accessories, no dialogue, no music.', NULL),
